---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { doctor, site } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Page
  title="Medical disclaimer"
  description="How to use the medical information published on this website, and its limits."
  slug="disclaimer"
  updated="2026-10-17"
  intro="This website publishes general medical information. It is written carefully, but it is not a substitute for being examined."
>
  <h2>General information, not personal advice</h2>
  <p>
    Everything published here — condition pages, treatment descriptions, diet charts and
    answers to common questions — is general education. It describes how conditions usually
    behave and what treatments usually involve. It does not describe your case.
  </p>
  <p>
    Skin and hair conditions that look similar are often different conditions, and the same
    condition behaves differently in different people. Nothing on this site should be used to
    diagnose yourself, to decide on a treatment, or to delay seeing a doctor.
  </p>

  <h2>No doctor–patient relationship</h2>
  <p>
    Reading this website does not create a doctor–patient relationship with {doctor.name} or with
    the clinics. That relationship begins only when you book and attend a consultation, in person
    or online.
  </p>

  <h2>Outcomes vary</h2>
  <p>
    No result is guaranteed. Response to treatment depends on the diagnosis, the severity, how
    long the condition has been present, other medical conditions, other medicines, and how
    consistently treatment is followed. Where a page describes a typical timeframe or a typical
    degree of improvement, that is an average across patients and not a promise to you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Patient reviews quoted on this site describe individual experiences. They are not a
    prediction of your outcome.
  </p>

  <h2>Medicines and procedures</h2>
  <p>
    Where this site names a medicine, it is describing treatments used in dermatology — not
    recommending that you take it. Prescription medicines should only be taken on the advice of a
    doctor who knows your history, and several of the medicines described carry important
    restrictions, including in pregnancy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not start, stop or change a prescribed medicine on the basis of anything read here.
  </p>

  <h2>When to seek care urgently</h2>
  <p>
    Do not rely on this website if you have a rash that is spreading rapidly, blistering, or
    accompanied by fever; a severe allergic reaction; a mole or growth that is changing; or any
    skin problem alongside feeling systemically unwell. Those need to be seen promptly and in
    person.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Where this site links elsewhere, those pages are not under our control and we are not
    responsible for their content or accuracy.
  </p>

  <h2>Review and accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    Clinical pages carry the date they were last reviewed. Medical understanding changes, and a
    page may not reflect the most recent evidence between reviews. If you believe something here
    is inaccurate, please write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> — corrections
    are welcome.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {doctor.name}, {doctor.qualifications}<br />
    {doctor.registration}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
  </p>
</Page>
